1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,520
Let go of me...
Stop it...

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,480
She's the only daughter we have left.

3
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,280
Did you kill Emma?

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,800
How dare you try to steal my daughter!

5
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,320
I'm going to kill you!

6
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:11,840
Elsa!

7
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Help!

8
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,480
Elsa!

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,680
Stay back!

10
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,520
Find an excuse and leave.

11
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:31,360
But...

12
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,680
Elsa...

13
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,640
The number you called cannot be connected.

14
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,760
Please call back later.

15
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,560
(Ngan Kai Bay Pier)

16
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,640
Why did Dr. Hong take three weeks off?

17
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,440
Dr. Hong didn't really say.

18
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,040
Please come this way.

19
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:09,760
Thanks.

20
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:16,640
Kwan Sir, looks very empty.

21
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,600
What do you know about his family?

22
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:23,520
He has a pretty wife and two daughters.

23
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,360
He has a family portrait.

24
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,720
He took it with him?

25
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,760
It's OK. Do you know their names?

26
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:34,560
I only know his wife is Mia.

27
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,640
The older daughter is Emma,

28
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,400
the younger one is Elsa.

29
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,600
Emma?

30
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,800
Emma Hong, Hong Ka-lam.

31
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:45,040
That's EH on the watchband.

32
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:49,160
C628, with the initials EH engraved
on the watchband.

33
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:52,000
Chan Lap-jim, James, right?

34
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:55,000
You're the faceless corpse Emma's boyfriend?

35
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:56,320
Yes.

36
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,320
A customer of the store said

37
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,560
he saw a tall man wearing
a dark green windbreaker

38
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:04,840
chasing someone like Emma near
where her body was found.

39
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,680
You have a similar build.

40
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,400
We also found on social media

41
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:11,440
you have a dark green windbreaker.

42
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,280
I'm not the only one who has it.

43
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,800
Emma's father has one too.

44
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,640
I'll get one for Daddy.

45
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,280
Good.

46
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,200
Why did Emma have to smuggle
out of Hong Kong?

47
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,360
She wanted to be in the UK with me.

48
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:26,880
But...she doesn't have an ID card.

49
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,520
As expected, she was undocumented.

50
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:31,680
What else did Emma say about her father?

51
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:34,000
Emma was very protective of her family.

52
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,160
I really don't know.

53
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:40,560
I remember...about six months ago,

54
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,760
Emma told me she had a chocolate cyst.

55
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:45,440
She said it hurt like hell.

56
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,280
I was worried about her

57
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,760
and told her to go see a doctor.

58
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,640
She told me not to worry

59
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,880
because her father will fix it.

60
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:58,480
Later, she told me it didn't hurt anymore.

61
00:03:58,600 --> 00:03:59,600
Chocolate cyst.

62
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:01,360
When we went to the hospital

63
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:05,040
to ask Hong Lik about the faceless corpse
and chocolate cyst,

64
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,520
he seemed very calm and composed.

65
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:09,280
But I noticed one thing,

66
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,200
when we showed him the picture
of the body,

67
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,200
he had a strong reaction.

68
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:17,400
As a doctor, he should be used to
something gory.

69
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:20,000
He shouldn't have looked so surprised.

70
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,960
The only reason for his reaction

71
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:24,880
was he knew we're talking about
his daughter.

72
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,440
No wonder the victim had no ID

73
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:31,520
but had access to prescription drugs
for her chocolate cyst.

74
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:35,200
Hong Lik and his family had so much to hide.

75
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,200
Based on Chan Lap-jim's statement,

76
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:42,040
I have reasons to believe Hong Lik
is a violent person

77
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:44,520
and an authoritative father.

78
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:47,840
To prevent exposing the family
for having no IDs,

79
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:51,280
he killed his rebellious older daughter.

80
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,240
Let's go to Ching Sir.

81
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,040
Where's my phone?

82
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:18,960
You're awake?

83
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:22,520
You haven't eaten in over ten hours.

84
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,800
You must be hungry. Eat this.

85
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,320
Why did you give me a shot?

86
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:27,920
Why did you tie me up?

87
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:30,720
You found out I had Emma's phone.

88
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:32,320
You must have a lot of questions

89
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,240
and won't come with us quietly.

90
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,400
But we must leave tonight.

91
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,880
I had no choice but to do this.

92
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:44,000
Did you kill Emma?

93
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,280
Whatever you want to know,

94
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,080
after we settle down,

95
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:51,240
I will tell you everything, OK?

96
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,280
If you won't tell me, you must have done it.

97
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:56,640
Why? How did you kill Emma?

98
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:58,240
She was your flesh and blood.

99
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,520
How could you do it?

100
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,360
Will you calm down? You just woke up,

101
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,120
I don't want to give you another shot.

102
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,080
Just listen to me and behave.

103
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:12,000
We're not far from where we should
board the boat.

104
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,240
Eat your food and get some rest

105
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,920
and get your strength back.

106
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,400
We'll be on the boat for a long time.

107
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,360
You creep! You killed Emma!

108
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,280
I'm not going with you.

109
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,800
It's very high!

110
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:23,760
Climb down!

111
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:24,520
It's so high!

112
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:26,960
We're dead if you don't.

113
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,840
Here goes nothing.

114
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,760
Elsa...

115
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:46,720
Elsa!

116
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:48,400
Elsa!

117
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,600
Elsa!

118
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:50,800
Wait here for me!

119
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,520
Elsa, come back!

120
00:07:55,640 --> 00:08:01,880
Elsa...

121
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,280
Help...

122
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,400
Elsa...stop running! Elsa!

123
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:29,360
Stay back!

124
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,880
Don't step back...it's dangerous!

125
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,680
Let me go...

126
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,880
Let me go, you creep!
Listen to me...

127
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:54,480
I'm not leaving with you.
Stop it, calm down...

128
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,800
I won't go with you.
Don't move!

129
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:56,760
Let go of me...

130
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,160
Stop it or I'll give you a shot.

131
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,080
Get me the needle...

132
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:01,240
Let go. She's the only daughter we have...

133
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,000
Mom!

134
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,240
You want to see this happen again?

135
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:07,040
Daddy killed Emma, right?

136
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:25,600
Mom, you knew about this?

137
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:29,760
You knew he killed Emma?

138
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:31,000
Elsa...

139
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,040
I'm asking you! Yes or no?

140
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,280
Are you crazy?

141
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,960
Emma was your daughter.

142
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:43,760
She only ran away from home,

143
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,920
why did you kill her?

144
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,080
And you lied to me!

145
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,720
Why do I have parents like you?

146
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,440
You killed your own daughter!

147
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,840
Tell me. Why did you kill Emma?

148
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,520
How did she die?

149
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,520
How did she die?

150
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:21,280
Emma's death had nothing to do with Mom.

151
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,920
Don't blame her.

152
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:35,120
The day Emma left,

153
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,640
I was anxious to find her.

154
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:44,920
I paid a hacker
to turn on her old phone

155
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:49,800
and found out she had a boyfriend
in the UK called James.

156
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:52,880
I figure since Emma didn't have an ID,

157
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,880
she couldn't possibly leave town legally.

158
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:57,440
Since she took so much money from me,

159
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,880
she's likely to smuggle to the UK

160
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,560
to be with her boyfriend.

161
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:06,400
I called up a patient from a few years ago
who's in the triad

162
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:10,240
to find out if Emma was leaving
on a speedboat.

163
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Three days after Emma left,

164
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:16,560
my triad friend finally found something.

165
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,560
Hello, Dr. Hong, I found out for you.

166
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,240
Tonight, a girl called Emma

167
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,920
will get on the boat from a pier
code named Meow Lung Kee.

168
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,760
Before they board the speedboat,

169
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:27,200
Meow Lung Kee will arrange for their
passengers to wait in Bo On Hotel

170
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,320
in Tsimshatsui.

171
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:31,680
So I looked for her at Bo On Hotel.

172
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,640
Is the girl in Room 3 around?

173
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,320
She went out.

174
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,640
Emma!

175
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:50,040
Emma...

176
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,240
Don't run!
Let go of me!

177
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:52,080
Come home with me...

178
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,600
That house is like a prison.

179
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:54,920
Nobody had any say in that house.

180
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,080
I don't want to be your slave.

181
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:56,720
Emma!

182
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,120
Help, he's trying to kidnap me!
Emma, come back!

183
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,480
Why are you chasing that girl?
You better watch it!

184
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:01,320
What do you want?
We're calling the Police...

185
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:04,080
I didn't want to make a scene in public.

186
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:06,000
So I decided to bring her home

187
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,640
before she boarded the boat at Meow Lung Kee

188
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:11,760
I know Meow Lung Kee is Ngan Kai Bay pier.

189
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:14,840
The boat wasn't there yet when
I arrived at the pier.

190
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,280
So I looked for Emma nearby

191
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:19,520
hoping to intercept her.

192
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:23,600
You're breaking up, reception is poor.

193
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,120
OK, bye!

194
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:35,440
Emma...come back!

195
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,200
Emma!
Stay back!

196
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:01,280
Don't move! Stop! It's dangerous!

197
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,680
I'd rather fall to death than
go home with you.

198
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,920
OK, I won't chase you...Come back in...

199
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,200
That's a lie. I don't believe you.

200
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:12,720
Emma...

201
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:16,080
Help me, Daddy!
I can't hold on...

202
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:19,040
Emma, grab my hand, don't let go. Emma...

203
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:21,440
I can't...

204
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,960
Emma...

205
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:32,880
Emma!

206
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,560
Emma...

207
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:45,920
Emma...are you OK?

208
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,080
It hurts...

209
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,120
Don't worry, let me examine you.

210
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,840
If I listened to you,

211
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:56,080
I wouldn't end up like this.

212
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:58,560
I'm sorry, Daddy!

213
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,840
My leg hurts.

214
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,000
Here?

215
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:07,760
It's a fracture. Should be nothing major.

216
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:10,960
Don't worry, I have a first aid kit
in the car.

217
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,240
I'll go get it.

218
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:14,720
Bear with me and wait here.

219
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:21,040
OK, I dressed your wound

220
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,040
and gave you a shot for the pain.

221
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,800
The pain is going away, right?

222
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:28,640
Daddy, I want to go home.

223
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:31,520
OK, I'll take you home.

224
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,600
Emma...

225
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:12,480
Emma...what happened?

226
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:13,200
Emma!

227
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,760
Emma is gone.

228
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:18,240
Emma, please don't die.

229
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:21,680
Emma, don't leave me, OK?

230
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:23,520
Emma...

231
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:26,920
Felix, how did Emma die?

232
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:33,040
Oh God!

233
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,320
We need to call the Police.

234
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,440
No Police!

235
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:49,360
What if they arrest you and Elsa?

236
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,800
I'll go buy some tools

237
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:58,320
and find a place to bury Emma.

238
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:03,200
Mom and I left Emma on the slope

239
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:05,040
and went to buy some tools.

240
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:08,240
But when we came back,

241
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:10,640
Emma's face was all torn up.

242
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:15,440
We also saw footprints of a wild boar.

243
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:19,040
I bet the wild boar chewed up her face.

244
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:22,080
I buried her by myself.

245
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:25,120
I gathered the money and took her phone...

246
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:34,080
and burnt everything else.

247
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,360
We didn't want to break your heart

248
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,200
and decided not to tell you.

249
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,520
I was afraid you'd call the Police.

250
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,840
I also wanted to buy some time

251
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:46,680
so I can take you and your Mom
away from Hong Kong.

252
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:51,440
I just didn't expect Emma's body
would be discovered so quickly.

253
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:53,920
What is it?

254
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:57,200
But you knew right away...

255
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,720
It's Emma.

256
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:01,360
...the faceless corpse was Emma.

257
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:06,640
I was afraid the Police will be
at our front door soon.

258
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:11,520
But then again, Emma's face
was all torn up

259
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:13,200
and her identity has not been documented.

260
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:16,480
The Police may not link her to us.

261
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,600
But I noticed you were texting Emma
on Chat App,

262
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:23,760
I guess you already suspect
Emma was dead.

263
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,880
To make you give up,

264
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:28,560
while you were cooking in the kitchen,

265
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,960
I asked Mom to use Emma's new phone

266
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:33,440
to text you saying she was safe.

267
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:35,680
It's Emma!

268
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:37,760
Then I stepped into the kitchen

269
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,720
and pretended I caught you
getting a message from Emma,

270
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:42,840
and told you to go tell your Mom.

271
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:46,400
She was emotionally unstable at the time.

272
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:48,720
I had to console her.

273
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,840
Luckily, you didn't catch on

274
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:53,440
and Mom and I were so relieved.

275
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:55,480
After the way things turned out,

276
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:58,240
I had to take you and Mom away ASAP.

277
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:01,520
I didn't expect the Police
to show up at the hospital

278
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:03,840
and ask me about the chocolate cyst.

279
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:08,400
Though I pretended I didn't recognize
the faceless corpse,

280
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:11,080
I knew the Police will catch on
sooner or later

281
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,920
I stole the drugs from the hospital

282
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,120
and gave them to Emma.

283
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:17,800
When the Police showed me Emma's picture,

284
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:21,120
it reminded me of how Emma died.

285
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:24,800
I felt as if I was stabbed in the heart.

286
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:31,280
If only Emma believed me,

287
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,680
none of this would have happened.

288
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:38,840
If you didn't pressure her and chase her,
she'd be fine.

289
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:41,360
You still don't think you were responsible?

290
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,360
Not that I don't think I'm responsible,

291
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,960
I just didn't expect
things to turn out like this.

292
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:51,920
Elsa, Daddy might have been strict
with you and Emma,

293
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:54,160
he only did it for your own good.

294
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:56,120
He already did all he could.

295
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,920
Emma is dead,

296
00:18:58,040 --> 00:19:00,000
have you any idea how heartbroken he was?

297
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:01,600
He couldn't sleep at night.

298
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:04,400
So? Heartbroken or not,

299
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,440
if he hadn't been so fierce with Emma,

300
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,680
she wouldn't be dead

301
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:09,800
and I wouldn't have lost my sister.

302
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:13,680
I hate you. I'll never forgive you.

303
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:16,000
Elsa, please!

304
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:18,360
I already lost Emma,

305
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:20,800
I can't lose you and your Daddy.

306
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,440
I don't want to live anymore.

307
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:25,280
Please don't leave me.

308
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:27,880
Please come with us.

309
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,920
I'm untying you.

310
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:49,360
We're boarding the boat at 8 o'clock.

311
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:53,760
It's a 30-minute walk from here
to the pier.

312
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:56,320
Then we'll be on the boat for a long time.

313
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,920
Get some rest.

314
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,440
I want my phone back.

315
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,840
I'll give it back when we land over there.

316
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:21,320
I just remember a hacker friend
recommended a tracker app.

317
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,960
Click this link...

318
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:28,040
click it and I can hack into your phone.

319
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,560
I'll know your location wherever you are.

320
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,720
Really? That's great!

321
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,280
Look!

322
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:37,360
You're right! That's great!

323
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:41,680
I have never seen anyone so happy
about being hacked.

324
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:52,640
(Ngan Kai Bay Pier)

325
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:58,400
Is Elsa locked up in here?

326
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:10,560
Police!

327
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:12,400
Police!

328
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:17,640
Kwan sir,

329
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:20,480
Hong Lik and his family
seem to have skipped town.

330
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:22,400
Ask Ching Sir to issue a warrant.

331
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:24,640
Let's check for any leads.

332
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:25,760
Yes, Sir!

333
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:10,880
Elsa...

334
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:16,880
I finally found you!

335
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:19,120
I thought I'll never see you again.

336
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,200
Did your father kill your sister?

337
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:24,720
Let's go.

338
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,600
No! I can't.

339
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:28,640
Your father will kill you too.

340
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,520
Emma's death was an accident.

341
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:32,880
Daddy didn't mean to kill her.

342
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,800
He's not heartless.

343
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:38,160
I promised Mom I'll go with her.

344
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:40,720
What are you doing here?

345
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:42,360
Elsa agreed to come with us.

346
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:43,680
How dare you try to steal my daughter!

347
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:45,280
I'm going to kill you!

348
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:47,680
Stop it...

349
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,080
No...

350
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,160
No...

351
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:51,480
YY won't hurt us...

352
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:52,640
Out of my way...

353
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:54,000
Elsa!

354
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:00,120
No!

355
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,840
Out of my way or I'll hit you too.

356
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,040
You already killed Emma.

357
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:04,240
I won't let you hurt YY.

358
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:05,360
Felix, stop it!

359
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:07,560
Elsa, get on the boat!
Mia...

360
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:10,120
YY, take care of Elsa.

361
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,560
No!

362
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:38,520
What?

363
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,440
Don't get on the boat!

364
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:40,160
Why?

365
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:42,120
If your Mom can't hold off your father,

366
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:44,200
or it was their act
to con you into boarding the boat,

367
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:45,520
you'll be in grave danger.

368
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:47,200
If I can't get on the boat

369
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,120
and I can't go home.

370
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:51,080
What should I do?

371
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:53,800
Let's get out of here.

372
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:58,480
They won't catch up with us.

373
00:24:58,560 --> 00:24:59,680
Let's sit down.

374
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:05,200
Well? Did Daddy hurt you?

375
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:06,760
I'm fine.

376
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:09,680
But your father was...

377
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:13,120
I have never seen him so ferocious!

378
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:16,960
The way I ran out on them,

379
00:25:17,080 --> 00:25:19,320
I may never see them again.

380
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:23,320
You still have me.

381
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:28,120
We'll be together, OK?

382
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:31,840
How? I have no ID.

383
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:36,520
Nobody knew about you before.

384
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,360
We can do it too.

385
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:43,920
Though I don't know what
our future holds,

386
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:48,120
I believe as long as we're together,

387
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:50,080
we won't have a problem.

388
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:54,040
Maybe we can be together...

389
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:59,800
for 10...20...30 years or even forever.

390
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:05,080
It'll be unfair to you,

391
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,840
when you're with me,

392
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:10,760
you'll need to live your life in the shadow.

393
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:15,560
As long as we're together,

394
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:18,360
nothing else matters.

395
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:43,200
After we finish eating,
we'll take a taxi to my place.

396
00:26:44,360 --> 00:26:46,560
You can sleep in my room.
I'll take the living room.

397
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:50,280
I'll get new furniture
so you can live more comfortably.

398
00:26:52,480 --> 00:26:55,440
Don't worry, I'll ease into it.

399
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:58,880
We have late breaking news.

400
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:02,160
Famous obstetrician and gynecologist
Dr. Hong Lik

401
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:04,360
has been arrested for the
murder of his daughter.

402
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:07,040
The Police confirmed his daughter

403
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:09,880
was the victim in the sensational
faceless corpse case.

404
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:13,920
Allegedly, the victim's identity and birth
have never been documented...

405
00:27:14,080 --> 00:27:14,960
What happened?

406
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:20,360
It's from Daddy.

407
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:22,400
How could he send me a message?

408
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:24,880
He must have pre-recorded a delayed message.

409
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:30,480
Elsa, when you get this recording,

410
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:33,680
you should be on the boat.

411
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,720
Earlier on,

412
00:27:38,840 --> 00:27:42,280
I saw on the surveillance app on my phone,

413
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,920
maybe because of Emma,

414
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:45,640
the Police already searched our house.

415
00:27:45,760 --> 00:27:48,320
They should soon find the village house.

416
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:49,680
What should we do now?

417
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:52,600
The key is to protect you and Elsa.

418
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:58,400
The cops want to arrest me because of Emma.

419
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:00,400
If they have me,

420
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:03,440
they probably won't come after you.

421
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:06,800
I saw the reporter climb upstairs.

422
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:08,760
He probably wanted to save Elsa.

423
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:13,120
Let him take you and Elsa on the boat.

424
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:14,560
I'm staying.

425
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:16,600
Let the Police arrest me too.

426
00:28:16,720 --> 00:28:18,240
I'm not afraid of going to jail.

427
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:20,160
I don't want Elsa involved.

428
00:28:20,320 --> 00:28:22,160
I know our daughter well.

429
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:25,760
She loves me. She won't leave with the boy.

430
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:28,640
I have an idea.

431
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:32,840
Find a chance to give this back to her.

432
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:35,880
Don't barge in so quickly. Wait a while.

433
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:40,840
What are you doing here?

434
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:42,520
Elsa agreed to come with us.

435
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:43,680
How dare you try to steal my daughter!

436
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:44,640
I'm going to kill you!

437
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:45,760
No, Daddy...

438
00:28:45,840 --> 00:28:47,440
After we're arrested,

439
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:51,040
the Police probably won't search nearby,

440
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:53,800
you should be safe.

441
00:28:54,240 --> 00:28:57,920
I hope this can buy you some time

442
00:28:58,040 --> 00:29:01,320
for you to board the boat safely.

443
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:03,120
Even if you can't get on the boat,

444
00:29:04,160 --> 00:29:06,600
when Mom and I turn ourselves in,

445
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:12,080
we should be able to get you
the status of a Hong Kong resident.

446
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:20,880
Anyway...you and Emma are the two people

447
00:29:21,040 --> 00:29:24,640
your Mom and I loved the most
in this world.

448
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:28,800
I'm willing to do anything for you.

449
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:34,640
Perhaps my way is not to your liking.

450
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:40,400
That's why we ended up like this.

451
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:44,080
I really regret it.

452
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:48,400
For over twenty years,

453
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:53,320
your Mom and I might have
made a lot of mistakes,

454
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:55,840
that's why we turned ourselves in

455
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:58,080
to get the punishment we deserved.

456
00:29:58,680 --> 00:30:01,120
Don't be unhappy.

457
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:09,360
The boy just now risked his life for you.

458
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:13,760
Your Mom and I are happy
to have him look after you.

459
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:17,440
Wherever you maybe,

460
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:21,760
I hope you'll always be happy.

461
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:25,200
Even if we never see you again,

462
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:29,360
we'll have nothing to worry about.

463
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:53,320
(Wise men say only fools rush in)

464
00:30:56,280 --> 00:31:07,920
(For I can't help falling in love with you)

465
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:24,320
(For I can't help falling in love with you)

466
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:39,920
(For I can't help falling in love with you)

467
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:55,520
Dr. Hong, you're suspected of murder.

468
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:57,360
You're now under arrest.

469
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:03,280
You have the right to remain silent.

470
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:05,920
Anything you wish to say
will be jotted down

471
00:32:06,080 --> 00:32:08,400
and may be used as evidence in court.

472
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:34,520
Miss Hong Ka-yee,

473
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,720
did the victim Hong Ka-lam

474
00:32:36,840 --> 00:32:39,360
often argue with her father Hong Lik?

475
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:42,480
And was locked up in her room by him
for almost a month?

476
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:45,680
Has Hong Lik been physically violent
towards her?

477
00:32:46,080 --> 00:32:51,520
Yes...right before my sister left home,

478
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:54,000
she often had fights with my father.

479
00:32:54,120 --> 00:32:55,760
But for over twenty years,

480
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:57,560
our family got along very well
with each other.

481
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:59,440
We almost never had any arguments.

482
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:01,920
How did you get along?

483
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:04,640
Our background is rather complicated.

484
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:10,280
Mom, my sister and I are undocumented.

485
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:15,760
My sister and I did not have
the freedom other kids have,

486
00:33:15,880 --> 00:33:17,680
we can't go to school

487
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:20,280
or borrow books from the library

488
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:22,480
or meet anyone we like.

489
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:26,320
But while we were growing up,

490
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:28,840
Daddy and Mom love us very much.

491
00:33:29,520 --> 00:33:31,520
Whatever we wanted,

492
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:33,680
they'd try hard to satisfy us,

493
00:33:34,120 --> 00:33:36,880
letting us learn different things.

494
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:39,360
Daddy is a doctor,

495
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:42,960
no matter how busy he was,

496
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:44,720
he tried to make time for us,

497
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:47,040
teaching us how to read and write

498
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:48,880
and played with us.

499
00:33:49,280 --> 00:33:52,400
My sister's death was a tragedy.

500
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:56,720
Though our childhood was different
from other kids,

501
00:33:58,280 --> 00:34:00,080
I felt I was fortunate enough

502
00:34:00,240 --> 00:34:02,200
to be born into a family like this

503
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:05,440
and grew up with my parents' love.

504
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:15,280
I'm sure my sister would think so too.

505
00:34:22,720 --> 00:34:27,200
Regarding the charge of manslaughter
of Hong Ka-lam by her father Hong Lik

506
00:34:27,320 --> 00:34:30,640
and the charge of preventing the lawful
burial of a body against Pak Mei-nga,

507
00:34:30,720 --> 00:34:33,040
will the Jury please give us your verdict?

508
00:34:35,640 --> 00:34:38,320
Your Honor, we have a unanimous verdict,

509
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:41,840
we find the first defendant Hong Lik
not guilty of manslaughter.

510
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:59,840
I can't believe you stayed.

511
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:03,760
I didn't know what you did was
for my own good.

512
00:35:04,880 --> 00:35:07,920
I thought you and Mom only loved each other.

513
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:11,240
I never expected, for my sake,

514
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:13,520
you'd stay behind and turn yourself in.

515
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:15,720
Now, you are forced to be apart.

516
00:35:15,840 --> 00:35:18,960
I let you down, I'm sorry.

517
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:21,760
You're my daughter,

518
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:25,520
I'll do anything for you.

519
00:35:26,440 --> 00:35:28,320
The same goes for your Mom.

520
00:35:28,640 --> 00:35:33,920
Luckily, you're both found guilty only of
preventing the lawful burial of a body

521
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:36,760
and not documenting our identities.

522
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:39,440
You'll be out in two years.

523
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,840
Two years will go by quickly.

524
00:35:42,360 --> 00:35:47,600
Actually...I should serve
more than two years.

525
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:53,040
Daddy, Emma's death was an accident.

526
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:54,960
Stop blaming yourself.

527
00:35:56,040 --> 00:36:00,480
No, I am responsible for her death.

528
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:02,000
Why?

529
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:05,600
I haven't told you the whole story.

530
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:07,600
Emma...
I can't hold on...

531
00:36:07,720 --> 00:36:10,200
Emma...

532
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:14,440
Emma...are you OK?

533
00:36:14,520 --> 00:36:15,760
It hurts...

534
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:17,920
Don't worry, let me examine you.

535
00:36:18,080 --> 00:36:20,560
It's a fracture. Should be nothing major.

536
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:21,800
No need to call the Police.

537
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:23,040
I can handle it.

538
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,840
Emma...

539
00:36:29,680 --> 00:36:34,000
Emma, why didn't I notice
you have internal bleeding?

540
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:36,720
I should have called an ambulance.

541
00:36:36,840 --> 00:36:39,440
I killed you, Emma...

542
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:43,640
I misjudged the severity of her condition.

543
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:45,640
If I had called an ambulance,

544
00:36:45,760 --> 00:36:48,000
Emma wouldn't have died.

545
00:36:48,160 --> 00:36:52,640
I was selfish and didn't want
the Police involved...

546
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,960
Your hands were shaking last time

547
00:36:55,160 --> 00:36:57,440
because you prescribed the wrong
drugs for a patient.

548
00:36:58,240 --> 00:37:01,040
It wasn't the guilt you felt towards
the patient,

549
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,920
but because it reminded you
of misjudging Emma's injuries.

550
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,680
After Emma died,

551
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:12,800
in order to hide the truth from you,

552
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:17,440
I refused to believe I killed her.

553
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:20,880
But deep down, I knew all along.

554
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:22,960
I killed your sister.

555
00:37:23,080 --> 00:37:27,920
Daddy, Emma was so seriously injured,

556
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:29,840
even if you called an ambulance,

557
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:31,520
she still couldn't have made it.

558
00:37:31,600 --> 00:37:33,360
The result would have been the same.

559
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,800
It's time you let it go.

560
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:42,400
Promise me.

561
00:37:43,720 --> 00:37:47,760
When Mom gets out, we can be reunited.

562
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:53,840
In the days ahead, you must
take care of yourself, OK?

563
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:55,840
OK!

564
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:05,400
YY helped me apply for proof of identity.

565
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:08,560
I can now openly walk down the streets.

566
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:12,240
It's OK, just fill this out for me...

567
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:14,960
Elsa, since you're scared.
You can sleep with me.

568
00:38:15,120 --> 00:38:15,760
Great!

569
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:17,920
QQ will keep you company too.

570
00:38:20,040 --> 00:38:22,720
Miss, you wish to apply for
this virtual credit card?

571
00:38:23,320 --> 00:38:26,360
If I apply for it, I'll get this suitcase?

572
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:28,880
Yes, but while stocks last.

573
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:29,800
I want to apply.

574
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:30,880
Please come this way.

575
00:38:30,960 --> 00:38:32,720
Your ID card please?

576
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:35,160
A photocopy?

577
00:38:35,240 --> 00:38:36,200
Yes...does that work?

578
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:37,160
It's OK...

579
00:38:37,600 --> 00:38:40,000
It's just a recognizance form.

580
00:38:40,640 --> 00:38:43,440
That's still proof of identity.

581
00:38:43,600 --> 00:38:44,560
Stop toying with us.

582
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:47,200
I should get my ID card soon.

583
00:38:47,320 --> 00:38:49,360
When you get your official ID card,

584
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:50,960
you can look us up.

585
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:53,040
But I really want this suitcase.

586
00:38:53,160 --> 00:38:55,360
I also want my own credit card.

587
00:38:55,480 --> 00:38:56,640
I will submit it later.

588
00:38:56,720 --> 00:38:57,640
Come back to us later.

589
00:38:57,720 --> 00:38:59,480
We'll wait for you.

590
00:38:59,560 --> 00:39:02,960
Sir, would you like to apply
for our virtual credit card?

591
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:11,320
(A few weeks later)

592
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:14,320
Hi, Emma.

593
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:20,480
I'm still not used to life without you.

594
00:39:22,600 --> 00:39:26,000
Mom is getting out in six months.

595
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:29,040
She'll be repatriated to her hometown.

596
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:32,800
But the Hong Kong government won't
restrict her from coming back.

597
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:37,360
She'll come back to Hong Kong
using the proper channels.

598
00:39:38,280 --> 00:39:41,040
When Daddy finished serving his
remaining 18 months,

599
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:44,160
we can be reunited.

600
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:46,160
I have another piece of good news.

601
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:48,720
Because I was born in Hong Kong,

602
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:54,480
and Daddy and Mom took so many
videos and pictures of us,

603
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:58,200
our piano teacher Miss Louise

604
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:00,560
and all our neighbors can vouch for me

605
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:03,720
that I have been living in Hong Kong
for many years,

606
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:06,480
Immigration used their discretion.

607
00:40:09,160 --> 00:40:10,080
See?

608
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:12,200
I finally have a Hong Kong ID card.

609
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:13,840
I'm officially a Hong Kong resident.

610
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:17,840
Emma, before you left home,

611
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:23,040
you said out here, you can go
anywhere you like

612
00:40:23,640 --> 00:40:26,960
and you promised to show me the world.

613
00:40:28,560 --> 00:40:33,720
The other day, someone was
promoting a credit card

614
00:40:33,840 --> 00:40:35,520
and they were giving away a suitcase

615
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:39,440
which had your favorite
cartoon character on it.

616
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:46,320
I thought if we could both have an ID card,

617
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:50,200
go on a trip together and start a new life,

618
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:52,000
wouldn't that be great?

619
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:56,800
I guess we'll never have the chance.

620
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:59,280
Because of your sacrifice,

621
00:41:00,520 --> 00:41:04,240
I now enjoy the happiness you want
me to have.

622
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:06,160
Thanks, Emma.

623
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:12,080
I'll always love you.

624
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:21,720
Did you find the band room?

625
00:41:21,800 --> 00:41:23,200
Shall I go with you?

626
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:24,840
I was on the wrong floor.

627
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:26,680
It should be the 9/F, don't worry.

628
00:41:26,760 --> 00:41:28,320
I found it. Get back to work.

629
00:41:28,440 --> 00:41:30,320
OK, be careful. Bye!

630
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:43,120
No...yes...push!

631
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:44,280
Two more steps...

632
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:45,960
1...2...

633
00:41:47,760 --> 00:41:49,280
Almost...

634
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:54,120
Stop! Gotcha!

635
00:41:54,440 --> 00:41:55,760
What is it, Miss?

636
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:58,160
You work for Bountiful Virtual Bank, right?

637
00:41:58,280 --> 00:42:00,560
You had a pop-up stand promoting
a credit card.

638
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:04,680
I went back there several times
but couldn't find you.

639
00:42:05,040 --> 00:42:06,960
Now I have my official ID card,

640
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:08,640
can I still apply for the credit card?

641
00:42:08,720 --> 00:42:10,480
Is the suitcase still available?

642
00:42:10,920 --> 00:42:13,200
The promotion is over. No more.

643
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:15,200
We'll call you next time.

644
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:17,240
Next time? When is that?

645
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,720
Will they still have the suitcase?

646
00:42:23,200 --> 00:42:24,720
Miss, you're too heavy.

647
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:26,000
Please step outside, OK?

648
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:27,160
Please?

649
00:42:27,240 --> 00:42:30,240
Heavy? Me? Not as heavy as your crate.

650
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:32,800
It's huge. What's inside?
